which would be the god-slaying weapon  that she was having huge create and  therefore combine them to forge a weapon  imbued with the power of the rune of  death capable of killing an outer god  however this is where ronnie comes into  play remember that ronnie claims to have  stolen a fragment of the rune of death  in order to create the black knives  through fearsome right so what if this  means that ronnie hijacked america's  plans and stole a fragment of the rune  of death and used it for her own rise to  power now i go into much more detail  regarding ronnie's full story in the  ronnie explain video so i won't explain  everything again here but remember that  ronnie is an emperian a pure blood  descendant of ratigan aka america the  newman and in my opinion that probably  means that ronnie herself was also a  newman she did show some strange  connections and knowledge of the eternal  cities and their hubris she knew of the  finger slayer blade's existence after  all and her associate eg wears a mirror  helm which is supposed to ward off  interference from the greater will and  is extremely similar to the nox mirror  helm which is also supposed to ward off  the greater will's interference and is  part of the nox set and you know who the  knox people are they are the very people  who long ago pissed off the greater will  and were banished too you guessed it the  eternal cities but you might be  wondering doesn't this mean that the  knox are the citizens of the eternal  cities and not the newman listen don't  be put off that some races of people  have multiple names like the nox  potentially being the newman or an older  version of them in the first place since  the new men are so rare and only pop up  every now and then it could be that they  are simply a specific bloodline or  family within the knox people and since  this game loves multiple names for the  same things like the erd tree probably  being the great tree or the dust guide  queen probably being the glomite queen  or rena being ronnie or margat being  morgut it is entirely possible that both  the knox and the new men could both come  from the lands underneath and are  therefore both connected to one another  geographically and in their defiance of  the greater will anyway it could be that  ronnie simply convinced the black knife  assassins her fellow newman to murder  her own body and godwin's soul in order  to aid in the rise of ronnie's age of  the stars perhaps the newman women began  to lose faith in queen america after so  many years of her apparent devotion and  complete service to the greater will  ronnie on the other hand promised  complete destruction of the greater will  and the golden order which is what the  knox and newman have wanted all along  and this may have been enough to  convince the black knife assassins to  follow through with her plans even if it  meant killing the innocent godwin i  think it's also interesting that  godwin's body turned up afterwards in  the unnamed eternal city which is where  the newman women might have called home  however i also think that the fact that  the black knife assassins showed up to  kill ronnie's associates eg and blythe  after her questline was done is very  important they must have lost faith in  ronnie and swung back to serving america  or the greater will at this point it's  not clear i'll admit this part has me  stumped because there are no pieces that  explain this but anyway the fact that  ronnie and godwin both died led to  america's legitimate dismay and forced  her hand into shattering the elden rings  since she no longer had a handle on the  rune of death which of course led to the  shattering war which led to the greater  will reviving the tarnish to quell the  nonsense and restore the elden ring and  the rest is playable history but the  newman no matter what you may believe  about the lore of the elden ring are  undoubtedly right in the middle of it  all and that my friends is my theory  about the women of newman and their  significance in the story as a whole but  what did you guys think are the newman  women from the eternal cities below and  did they really betray america by  following ronnie's orders to assassinate  godwin or is this all just a bunch of  baseless speculation and the women of  newman really are just aliens from  another planet let me know in the  comments below also thank you so much  for watching if you enjoyed it or at  least my efforts into making it please  consider leaving a like on the video as  these videos take lots of time and brain  power to put together and subscribe if  you haven't already for many more lore  videos to come huge thanks as always to  my bandit crew of which i have the  fabulous xander bee to welcome into the  fold that's all i've got for this one so  as always i hope you have a wonderful  rest of your day this is bandit looking  forward to seeing you next time and  signing out peace  [Music]  you
 

